WEBVTT

00:31:26.882 --> 00:31:30.826
that the louder and the more insistent
an organization was

00:31:30.850 --> 00:31:32.708
about bringing your whole self to work,

00:31:32.732 --> 00:31:34.916
almost the less work they'd done

00:31:34.940 --> 00:31:37.076
to make that actually possible.

00:31:37.100 --> 00:31:40.188
AG: People who don't fit
the dominant culture in an organization

00:31:40.212 --> 00:31:41.375
learn the hard way

00:31:41.399 --> 00:31:44.896
that they sometimes have to hide
their authentic identities and ideas.

00:31:44.920 --> 00:31:46.946
They try to fit into that expectation,

00:31:46.970 --> 00:31:49.326
intentionally or subconsciously,

00:31:49.350 --> 00:31:51.513
even though it doesn't feel right.

00:31:52.367 --> 00:31:55.040
Let's say the conformity pressure
you're feeling at work

00:31:55.064 --> 00:31:58.076
is about norms and values,
not cultural stereotypes.

00:31:58.100 --> 00:32:00.847
How do you break through
that pressure and get heard